    "summary": "RedHatAI's W4A16 Qwen3.5-9B served by vLLM XPU on one B70 through the lab's R276 image, with the publisher's MTP head as a lossless speculative draft. vLLM's compressed-tensors path selects the lab's wNa16 INT4 kernel, whose fixed-K two-tier strategy is row-count invariant: without speculation this route is byte-exact against a single request at every concurrency through 64 users, where the FP8 route on the same model flips a near-tie token from 16 users up. It is also 28% faster without speculation and 15% faster with it. The kernel is not the only reduction on that path: the RMSNorm this route runs is itself row-count dependent (measured 2026-09-08), so the route is exact in the regimes measured rather than exact by construction.",
